**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SceneSaveLoadTests`

**How to implement.** A kit opened read-only refuses every write message, and the controls that send them are withheld (the S5.3 brief: read-only shows in the title and disables every write message; step 155: a window opened read-only answers `KitReadOnlyErr` in its `kitStatus`, and S5.3 disables those messages; .spec-md §3.12: a read-only open writes nothing). The write messages are those whose arms write the kit: `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove` and `AttachDataFileTo` (step 152) and `SceneSave` (step 153). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: on the extension that holds `kitCaption` (step 184), `member model.kitWrites : ControlAvailability` answers `ControlOffered` for `ReadWriteKitAccess` and `ControlWithheld` for `ReadOnlyKitAccess` (`RotationControls.fs:19`), the one place the kit's access decides a control. In `updateTableAndElementRotation`, each of the four write messages first matches `model.kitWrites`: `ControlWithheld` answers the model unchanged except `kitStatus = Some (ControlCaption "The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.")`, calls no proxy and writes nothing; `ControlOffered` runs the arm steps 152 and 153 wrote, unchanged. One private function holds that guard, and the four arms call it. Every other message, the draft's and `SceneLoad` included, is unchanged. (2) The view withholds those controls under `ControlWithheld`. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/ExperimentControls.fs`: `ExperimentControlsState` gains `removalAvailability : ControlAvailability` after `addAvailability` (`ExperimentControls.fs:227`), documented in one line (whether a collected experiment's Remove is offered), `ControlOffered` in `emptyExperimentControls` (`:248`); `rowActionButton` (`:727`) takes a `ControlAvailability` after its background and sets `Border.isEnabled` and the 0.4 opacity of a withheld box as `actionButton` (`:696`) does; `collectionRow` (`:745`) takes the availability its Remove passes, its View passing `ControlOffered`; and `collectionBlock` passes `state.removalAvailability`. (b) In `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, the experiment-controls state the Experiments bay builds sets `addAvailability` to `ControlWithheld` when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld` and to today's rule otherwise, and `removalAvailability` to `model.kitWrites`. `attachDataFileButton` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3419`) takes `model.kitWrites` and, withheld, sets `Border.isEnabled` false and opacity 0.4 and opens no picker. `workbenchButton` (`:3237`) becomes a call of a new private `availableWorkbenchButton (availability : ControlAvailability)` with `ControlOffered`, so one body draws both, and the scene row's `Save scene` (step 153) is `availableWorkbenchButton model.kitWrites`. No other control is withheld, and nothing is hidden: a read-only window shows what the kit holds. (3) Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 184) gains `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`: a kit holding experiment `E1` (written through `writeExperiment`, step 148) and closed is opened read-only and loaded into `initMain ()`; with a draft ready to commit (a linear polarizer added and chosen, as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:filledExperiments` builds one), `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove (ExperimentId 1)`, `AttachDataFileTo` of `ExperimentId 1` and a data file under the fact's folder, and `SceneSetName (ControlCaption "Bench")` then `SceneSave` each leave the experiments and `savedScenes` as they were and set `kitStatus` to `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.`, and every file of the folder keeps its bytes. `a kit's access decides whether its writes are offered`: `kitWrites` is `ControlOffered` for the kit opened read-write and `ControlWithheld` for it opened read-only. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs`: `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why` (step 152) keeps its assertions over a model whose kit's proxy is `readOnlyView` and whose `access` stays `ReadWriteKitAccess`, so the write still reaches the proxy and fails there; only its fixture line changes. `KitWindowTests` (step 184) gains `a read-only window withholds every write control`: `mainView` mounted as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` mounts a view (`:107`), over the inverse model (`initInverse`, so the Data files section shows) loaded from a kit holding `E1` opened read-only, with the Experiments bay selected and a draft ready to commit: `experimentAddButton`, the `experimentRemoveButton` and the `attachDataFile` of `E1`, and `saveSceneButton` are disabled; over the same kit opened read-write they are enabled.

**Acceptance.** After the read-only gate lands, under `ReadOnlyKitAccess` the messages `ExpCommit`, `ExpRemove`, `AttachDataFileTo` and `SceneSave` MUST answer the read-only status and write nothing, and the controls sending them MUST be withheld; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` and `a kit's access decides whether its writes are offered`, the count rising by 2; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a read-only window withholds every write control` and `a kit write that fails keeps the experiment and shows why`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
